TIP:  The easiest way I found to pick those first three notes of the mandolin intro is to start with your index finger on the 3rd string/2nd fret <a>.  Pick the <a> and the open 2nd string <b> just below it, and then drop your index finger down to cover the 2nd string and pick the <f#>, then release and form the first (D).

TIP:  The song has a very quick tempo to it and it’ll help to think like a mandolin player, with short quick strums. 
    

